2531-      "negationNote": "Identifiers the ceremony must NOT touch do appear in the node's text - that is how an exclusion is stated - so the gate requires every CLAUSE that mentions one to carry a negation marker, rather than requiring absence. Attribution is per clause, not per character window: AC4 states its exclusion AFTER the identifiers it excludes, so a preceding-context check would miss the real text, while a window wide enough to reach backwards over a list of four App IDs is also wide enough to let a neighbouring clause's 'NOT' cover an identifier that has quietly become authorized. An r7 board negative gate demonstrated exactly that against a 220-character symmetric window, which is why the window was replaced by clause attribution. Clause splitting is safe despite these identifiers being full of dots, because a dot INSIDE an identifier is never followed by whitespace.",
